cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use omnibias in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "omnibias: numerically-stable closed-form n-th derivative forward-pass framework"
abstract: >-
  omnibias computes the closed-form n-th derivative of an activation,
  sigma^(n)(z), for arbitrary n with bit-stable accuracy and a single sigma
  evaluation regardless of order. The same primitive is exposed on PyTorch,
  JAX, and Keras 3 from one shared pure-Python coefficient core, so every
  backend is bit-identical by construction. The core math is the Riccati
  identity plus the Eulerian / Legendre / Hermite polynomial recurrences it
  implies, extended to multi-layer and multivariate Taylor jets via Bell /
  Faa di Bruno combinatorics.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Grigoryants"
    given-names: "Vardan"
    affiliation: "Derivon"
    email: "vardan@derivon.ai"
